       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Scope of practice:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a PA’s scope of practice is based on their education, training, experience and competency, and includes the professional activities they are qualified and authorized to perform."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "AAPA’s position:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " AAPA advocates for the full removal of any legal requirement for a PA to be supervised by a specific provider, and supports collaborative, team-based care determined at the practice level."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Collaboration agreements:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " when the supervision requirement is removed, state laws and regulations may require a collaboration agreement between PAs and other providers."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "States with no required physician relationship:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Delaware, Iowa, Maine, Montana, New Hampshire, North Dakota, South Dakota, Utah, Virginia and Wyoming have eliminated the legal requirement for a specific relationship between a PA and a physician or any other healthcare provider."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Optimal Team Practice (OTP):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " an AAPA policy adopted in May 2017 that seeks laws authorizing PAs to practice to the full extent of their education, training and experience absent a mandated relationship to a specific healthcare provider, PA participation in regulating the profession, and direct payment of PAs by all public and private insurers."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
